--- body ---
## Context

Each source module exposes `fetch_pdf(doi, title, output_dir)` and returns a free-form dict with
`status` in `success|failed|skipped` plus whichever of `doi`, `title`, `file_name`, `error`, `url` it
chooses. `fetch.py:_fetch_one` dispatches by convention only: `fetch_url.fetch_pdf` takes a URL in the
`doi` slot, ISBNs arrive as `isbn:` strings, `source == "all"` returns the last failure. Nothing states
what a fetcher may assume, must return, or may raise, so each new source (and each fix to 0004's
naming) re-derives it.

After 0004 (the caller decides the file name) and 0006 (sources live in `doifetch/sources/`), the
contract can be written once.

## Actions
1. The contract is data and a function signature, not a class hierarchy: no ABC, no base class, no
   `Protocol` to inherit or implement. A source stays a plain module.
   `doifetch/sources/contract.py` holds only:
   - frozen dataclasses `Request` (identifier kind DOI/ISBN/URL, the identifier, target path decided by
     the caller) and `Result` (`status`, `source`, `path`, `error`, `detail_url`), `status` a `Literal`;
   - the type alias `Fetch = Callable[[Request], Result]`;
   - the contract rules, in the module docstring.
2. Each source module exposes `NAME: str`, `ACCEPTS: frozenset[Kind]` and `def fetch(req: Request) -> Result`.
3. Contract rules: never raises into the fetch loop (errors become `status="failed"` with a reason);
   writes only `req.path`; never leaves a partial file; returns `success` only for a file that passed
   the PDF check.
4. The registry in `cli.py` is a typed table `dict[str, Fetch]` built from the modules; dispatch reads
   `ACCEPTS`, not string prefixes.
5. Enforcement is by the type checker (mypy or pyright, lenient, on `src/doifetch/sources/`, in
   0007's gate) and by 0009's conformance suite, not by inheritance.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every source exposes `NAME`, `ACCEPTS`, `fetch`; no class in `sources/`; the type checker passes
- [ ] `cli.py` has no per-source special case
- [ ] Behaviour unchanged on the existing suite
- [ ] Public library API: `from doifetch import Request, Result, fetch` is the stable import path;
      `doifetch.fetch(req)` runs the default source cascade, not one source
- [ ] `import doifetch` has no side effects and needs no extra: no network, no prompt (Firefox cookie,
      ISTEX), no optional dependency imported; a test imports it with the extras absent
